{"id":"bc6b982512ea7cbd","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-thm-analytic-set-properties.md","title":"Analytic Set Properties","display":"thm-analytic-set-properties — Analytic Set Properties","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-analytic-set-properties","aliases":["58-thm-analytic-set-properties","Analytic Set Properties","$\\Sigma^1_1$ Properties"],"display":"thm-analytic-set-properties — Analytic Set Properties","depends_on":["[[../batch01/58-df-zfc-desc-analytic-set.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-lebesgue-measurable.md]]","[[./58-df-countable.md]]","[[../batch08/58-df-perfect.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-reals.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-analytic-set-properties"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-analytic-set-properties</span><span>Analytic Set Properties</span><span><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma^1_1\">\\(\\Sigma^1_1\\)</span> Properties</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-analytic-set-properties — Analytic Set Properties"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"2631de10a773dc04\" href=\"?note=2631de10a773dc04\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-zfc-desc-analytic-set.md\">../batch01/58-df-zfc-desc-analytic-set.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"3b8b3b1a1bbba5e8\" href=\"?note=3b8b3b1a1bbba5e8\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-lebesgue-measurable.md\">../batch09/58-df-lebesgue-measurable.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"1b3610e6aed65b25\" href=\"?note=1b3610e6aed65b25\" title=\"./58-df-countable.md\">58-df-countable.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" href=\"?note=f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-perfect.md\">../batch08/58-df-perfect.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"c54af6fc6a780954\" href=\"?note=c54af6fc6a780954\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-reals.md\">../batch02/58-df-reals.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,P\\subseteq\\mathbb R\">\\(A,P\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathbb R},d_{\\mathbb R}\\in V\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathbb R},d_{\\mathbb R}\\in V\\)</span> are the usual topology and metric (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"c54af6fc6a780954\" href=\"?note=c54af6fc6a780954\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-reals.md\">../batch02/58-df-reals.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcDescAnalyticSet}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcDescAnalyticSet}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"2631de10a773dc04\" href=\"?note=2631de10a773dc04\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-zfc-desc-analytic-set.md\">../batch01/58-df-zfc-desc-analytic-set.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S,\\mathrm{Countable}_S\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S,\\mathrm{Countable}_S\\subseteq V\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Perfect}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Perfect}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"3b8b3b1a1bbba5e8\" href=\"?note=3b8b3b1a1bbba5e8\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-lebesgue-measurable.md\">../batch09/58-df-lebesgue-measurable.md</a>, <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"1b3610e6aed65b25\" href=\"?note=1b3610e6aed65b25\" title=\"./58-df-countable.md\">58-df-countable.md</a>, <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" href=\"?note=f6afc84fe5b2b44e\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-perfect.md\">../batch08/58-df-perfect.md</a>, <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-12\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}analytic\\text{-}set\\text{-}properties} \\vdash\n\\forall A\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{ZfcDescAnalyticSet}_S(A,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R})\\to\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S(A)\\land\n(\\mathrm{Countable}_S(A)\\lor\\exists P\\subseteq A\\;\\bigl(P\\neq\\emptyset\\land\n\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\land\n\\mathrm{Perfect}_S(P,\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\bigr))\\bigr)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}analytic\\text{-}set\\text{-}properties} \\vdash\n\\forall A\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{ZfcDescAnalyticSet}_S(A,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R})\\to\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasurable}_S(A)\\land\n(\\mathrm{Countable}_S(A)\\lor\\exists P\\subseteq A\\;\\bigl(P\\neq\\emptyset\\land\n\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\land\n\\mathrm{Perfect}_S(P,\\mathbb R,d_{\\mathbb R})\\bigr))\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Analytic sets can be characterized as continuous images of Borel sets, equivalently by the Souslin operation on closed sets.</li>\n<li>Every analytic set is Lebesgue measurable.</li>\n<li>Every analytic set has the perfect set property in the explicitly supplied Euclidean metric, hence is either countable or of size continuum.</li>\n<li>Foundation: for projective hierarchy.</li>\n<li>Suslin: discovered analytic sets (1917).</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch01/58-df-zfc-desc-analytic-set.md","status":"resolved","id":"2631de10a773dc04","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-zfc-desc-analytic-set.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-lebesgue-measurable.md","status":"resolved","id":"3b8b3b1a1bbba5e8","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-lebesgue-measurable.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"./58-df-countable.md","status":"resolved","id":"1b3610e6aed65b25","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[./58-df-countable.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-perfect.md","status":"resolved","id":"f6afc84fe5b2b44e","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-perfect.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-reals.md","status":"resolved","id":"c54af6fc6a780954","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-reals.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-reals.md","status":"resolved","id":"c54af6fc6a780954","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$A,P\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ and $\\tau_{\\mathbb R},d_{\\mathbb R}\\in V$ are the usual topology and metric (see [[../batch02/58-df-reals.md]]).","embed":false},{